WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.437
Two agents edit the same dispute note on their laptops, both offline.

2
00:00:07.437 --> 00:00:08.879
The note says pay 40.

3
00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:11.890
Agent a types a dollar sign before the 4.

4
00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:14.989
Agent b types an exclamation mark at the end.

5
00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:22.213
The simplest edit names a position: insert dollar sign at 4, and insert exclamation mark at 6.

6
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.933
Back online, they swap.

7
00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:29.133
Agent b puts the dollar sign at position 4, and gets the text they both meant.

8
00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:32.706
Agent a puts the exclamation mark at position 6.

9
00:00:32.706 --> 00:00:38.819
But a's text grew by one in front of that spot, so 6 now falls between the 4 and the 0.

10
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.643
Now the copies differ.

11
00:00:40.643 --> 00:00:45.947
Position 6 meant after the 0 to agent b, and something else to agent a.

12
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.338
Start again with a sequence CRDT, which never sends a position.

13
00:00:50.338 --> 00:00:56.460
Each character gets a permanent id when it's typed: a counter, plus the site that typed it.

14
00:00:56.667 --> 00:01:02.095
Agent a's dollar sign becomes 7a, inserted after 4a, the space.

15
00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:06.835
Agent b's exclamation mark becomes 7b, after 6a, the 0.

16
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:07.894
Swap again.

17
00:01:07.894 --> 00:01:14.075
At agent a, the exclamation mark goes right after 6a, wherever 6a has moved.

18
00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:17.485
At agent b, the dollar sign goes after 4a.

19
00:01:17.485 --> 00:01:19.784
Both copies now read the same.

20
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.016
Order doesn't matter either.

21
00:01:22.016 --> 00:01:29.144
A third copy, copy c, hears agent b's edit first and agent a's second, and ends with the same text.

22
00:01:29.333 --> 00:01:34.631
If two inserts follow the same character, every copy puts the bigger id first.

23
00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:37.140
The price is the ids, kept forever.

24
00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:42.411
A deleted character stays as a tombstone, because a late edit may still name it.

25
00:01:42.411 --> 00:01:45.904
In the lab, that cost 17 bytes per visible character.

26
00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:53.125
Name every character, never a position, and every copy that sees the same edits ends with the same text.
